# .dockerignore — what never enters a build context of this repository
# (infrastructure.md §2.3). Smaller context = faster builds, but the first
# reason is safety: .env, local IDE state and the archive must not be baked
# into an image by accident.
#
# The platform image (build/Dockerfile) builds ./cmd/... of the root module and
# copies the data directories (blueprints/, rules/, laws/, config/), so *.md is
# deliberately NOT excluded — blueprints are data, not documentation.

# --- VCS, CI and team artifacts ---
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
Docs/
plans/
reports/
memory/
PULL_REQUEST.md

# --- Secrets and local configuration (never in an image) ---
.env
.env.*
**/.env.*
!.env.example
.mcp.env
.mcp.env.example
.mcp.json
.claude/
.qwen/
.gigacode/
.kilo/
.kilocode/
.kilocodemodes
.roo/
.roomodes
.idea/
.vscode/
.ai/

# --- Separate Go modules: not part of the root module, not in the image ---
# services/ holds the 8 frozen services (FROZEN.md) and services/_archive/**
# (U-1: archived, never deleted). The `legacy` profile builds its own images
# from build/legacy.Dockerfile; when T-008 wires that profile up it must give
# the build its own context or re-include the two directories it needs here.
services/

# --- Build artifacts, data and local runtime state ---
bin/
dist/
backups/
ops/
testdata/recordings/
coverage.*
**/coverage.*
*.exe
**/*.exe
*.test
**/*.test
*.out
**/*.out
*.log
**/*.log
*.db
**/*.db
*.db-wal
**/*.db-wal
*.db-shm
**/*.db-shm

# --- OS noise ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
